From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: imx95-mipi-dsi: round htotal to whole lane byte
 clocks

In non-burst video mode the dw-mipi-dsi core programs DSI_VID_HLINE_TIME
as htotal * bpp / (lanes * 8) lane byte clocks, rounded up. When that is
not a whole number, every DSI line is slightly longer than the DPI line
from the display controller, the two drift apart over the frame and the
picture is corrupted.

The i.MX 93/8 glue (dw_mipi_dsi-imx.c) works around this only for a list
of CEA modes. Do it generally in the i.MX 95 mode_fixup: stretch the
front porch until the line is a whole number of lane byte clocks.

Seen on the Cargt i.MX 95 00414 SOM with the GLT0557201280IS1 720x1280
ILI9881C panel (htotal 870, 4 lanes, RGB888 = 652.5 lane byte clocks):
the picture was corrupted until htotal became 872 (654), confirmed on
hardware with a custom mode of exactly that timing.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/imx/imx95-mipi-dsi.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/imx/imx95-mipi-dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/imx/imx95-mipi-dsi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/imx/imx95-mipi-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/imx/imx95-mipi-dsi.c
@@ -185,6 +185,7 @@
 	unsigned int lane_mbps;
 	bool use_pl0;
 	enum mipi_dsi_pixel_format format;
+	unsigned long mode_flags;
 	struct dw_mipi_dsi *dmd;
 	struct dw_mipi_dsi_plat_data pdata;
 	union phy_configure_opts phy_cfg;
@@ -954,8 +955,36 @@
 	memcpy(adjusted_mode, mode, sizeof(*mode));
 	adjusted_mode->clock = rounded_rate / 1000;
 
-	dev_dbg(dsi->dev, "adj clock %d for mode " DRM_MODE_FMT "\n",
-		adjusted_mode->clock, DRM_MODE_ARG(mode));
+	/*
+	 * Cargt: in non-burst video mode the dw-mipi-dsi core programs the
+	 * line time (DSI_VID_HLINE_TIME) as htotal * bpp / (lanes * 8) lane
+	 * byte clocks, rounded up. When that is not a whole number the DSI
+	 * line is longer than the DPI line, the two drift apart over each
+	 * frame and the picture is corrupted. Stretch the front porch until
+	 * the line is a whole number of lane byte clocks. This is the
+	 * generalization of the CEA-mode htotal workaround in
+	 * dw_mipi_dsi-imx.c (i.MX 93/8); e.g. the 720x1280 GLT0557201280IS1
+	 * panel (htotal 870, 4 lanes, RGB888) becomes htotal 872.
+	 */
+	if (!(dsi->mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST) && dsi->lanes) {
+		int bpp = mipi_dsi_pixel_format_to_bpp(dsi->format);
+		unsigned int div = dsi->lanes * 8;
+		unsigned int pad = 0;
+
+		while (bpp > 0 && pad < div &&
+		       ((adjusted_mode->htotal + pad) * bpp) % div)
+			pad++;
+
+		if (bpp > 0 && pad < div && pad) {
+			adjusted_mode->hsync_start += pad;
+			adjusted_mode->hsync_end += pad;
+			adjusted_mode->htotal += pad;
+			drm_mode_set_crtcinfo(adjusted_mode, 0);
+		}
+	}
+
+	dev_dbg(dsi->dev, "adj clock %d htotal %d for mode " DRM_MODE_FMT "\n",
+		adjusted_mode->clock, adjusted_mode->htotal, DRM_MODE_ARG(mode));
 
 	return true;
 }
@@ -1105,6 +1134,7 @@
 
 	dsi->lanes = device->lanes;
 	dsi->format = device->format;
+	dsi->mode_flags = device->mode_flags;
 
 	return 0;
 }
-- 
